- Story & Context: Sarita, the fishmonger with eyes like polished river stones, found an ancient, waterlogged cassette tape buried beneath her stall; when she played it on her grandmother's clunky, salvaged boombox, it whispered her own unuttered regrets about a lost love, prompting a public, tear-soaked admission at the market. "I heard my own foolish heart on that warped tape," she confessed to the grandmothers, her voice cracking as the first rays of sun hit the wet market planks.
