Track 3: Gulls & Glyphs of the Skipping Disc
- Story & Context: Young Jom, who thought the old stories were just superstitions, was dared to play a scratched, skipping vinyl record found in the grandmothers' hidden collection, and as the needle jumped, a flock of unusually large, silent gulls descended upon the market, their shadow-shapes forming intricate, shifting patterns on the market's tarps, revealing ancient prophecies. "The skipping truth will find its landing," the grandmothers chanted softly, as Jom watched, mesmerized, the gulls' movements predicting the next morning's tide.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A fragmented, scratched vinyl record, its grooves distorted into abstract glyphs, reflecting the stark, silhouetted forms of giant, almost prehistoric-looking gulls circling overhead against a bruised, early morning sky.

